<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Berlin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1949–1990</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> was the western part of Berlin, formed from the American, British and French occupation sectors of the city, an enclave surrounded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-germany">East Germany</a> from 1949 to 1990. It survived the Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naval-blockade">blockade</a> of 1948–1949 through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-airlift">Berlin Airlift</a> and was closely tied to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a>, though formally under Allied authority. From 1961 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin-wall">Berlin Wall</a> cut it off from East Berlin until the Wall fell in 1989.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-berlin.jpg" alt="West Berlin" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flaggenentwurf: unbekannt diese Datei: Jwnabd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Berlin.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
